### Additional Use Grant

You may use the Licensed Work in production, provided your use does not include
any of the following:

1. **Offering a Competing Service.** You may not offer the Licensed Work, or
   any derivative or substantial portion of it, to third parties as a hosted or
   managed browser-diagnostics, error-tracking, session-replay, real-user
   monitoring, or support-capture service that competes with hosted
   observability offerings. This includes any product whose primary value to
   its users is capturing or exporting end-user browser sessions or network
   diagnostics.

2. **Resale or Redistribution as a Standalone Product.** You may not sell,
   license, or distribute the Licensed Work, or any derivative or fork of it,
   as a standalone commercial product.

3. **Removal of Attribution.** Any derivative work, fork, or redistribution of
   the Licensed Work must prominently credit AbsoluteJS and include a link to
   the original project repository (https://github.com/absolutejs/diagnostics).

For clarity, the following uses are expressly permitted:

- Using the Licensed Work to diagnose your own applications, websites,
  internal tools, or SaaS products.
- Using the Licensed Work as a dependency in commercial software, provided
  that diagnostics is not the primary product being sold.
- Providing consulting, development, or support services using the Licensed
  Work.
- Forking and modifying the Licensed Work for internal use, with attribution.

